[RESUME] p2 headline (from its own log, to be confirmed by its validator):
     U-U-U-A-U is the best hetero schema -- test Hit@1 0.6163, MRR 0.7362, country test
     micro-F1 0.7887 -- beating p1's best homogeneous country micro-F1 (0.7661).
     Pure U-A-U is much WORSE than social-only (test MRR 0.589 vs 0.725): the artist
     layer is 155x denser than the social layer, so an unconstrained U-A-U step is
     mostly noise. The striking one: at source degree 0 (cold start), val Hit@1 goes
     from ~0.06 in Task 3 to ~0.46 with artist edges -- which is precisely the
     cold-start bottleneck p1 concluded no walk strategy could fix. The two fragments
     therefore tell one coherent story, which is what I grouped them to achieve.

